usage: bounded_launcher.py [-h] --candidate CANDIDATE --output OUTPUT
                           [--optimized] [--manufactured-only]
                           ...

Nonroot custodian for the registered, offline endpoint worker. The worker is
exec'd before it installs seccomp after numeric imports. The custodian imports
no numerical dependency, authenticates first, applies exact hard rlimits
before exec, and records the authoritative Linux wait4 outcome. Aggregate
output is polled and checked again after exit; it is an acceptance limit, not
a filesystem quota. No physical authorization is created here.

positional arguments:
  worker_arguments      After --, supply registration and optional physical
                        GO/repository arguments

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --candidate CANDIDATE
  --output OUTPUT
  --optimized
  --manufactured-only
